From: GPT-6.1-Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: bind retirement to queued and in-flight flushes

Resolve the three outstanding handoff-review findings in 0185. Assign a
monotonic per-CRTC update generation under commit_lock before programming,
including coalesced async updates. Keep sync commit_lock through wait_flush
so a completion cannot accidentally acknowledge a later submission. Retired
buffers wait for the required generation and a frozen subsequent vblank;
newer flushes never advance that target. A failed vblank rearm retains the
listed pin for the hardware-off drain. Allocation/initial schedule failure
cannot use a pre-flush vblank as proof: retain the pin if a flush is pending.

Local correction to the v3 deferred-release proposal in 0184/0185.
Hardware: double-buffer reuse, async cursor updates stalled before flush,
dual-display flips and DPMS/hotplug; no SMMU faults or steadily growing pins.
Fault injection: allocation and vblank enable/rearm failures, then disable.

